cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Agent Ready GEO, please cite it as below."
title: "Agent Ready GEO: an agent skill that makes a website agent-ready"
abstract: >-
  Agent Ready GEO is an agent skill for Claude Code, Codex and other clients
  that load Agent Skills. It reads a website's score on isitagentready.com and
  builds the missing pieces on the site's own hosting: robots.txt rules for AI
  crawlers and Content Signals, a sitemap, Link headers, Markdown for agents,
  llms.txt and llms-full.txt, an API catalog and OpenAPI document, a running
  MCP server and its server card, an Agent Skills index whose digests match the
  served bytes, WebMCP browser tools, ARD, OAuth discovery and auth.md, DNS-AID
  records and, where the site signs its own requests, Web Bot Auth. Capabilities
  presented as available have to work; anything not built yet is published only
  as a labeled coming-soon declaration the site owner approves. The skill's
  instructions are written in iLang and pass the iLang grammar validator; the
  read-only probe and the artifact verifier are Python 3.9 standard library only
  and ship with their tests.
type: software
